course: dictionary
lesson: 5897
title: Mapping: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and mapping is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Great Britain's national mapping agency, Ordnance Survey, began in 1791 and makes detailed maps at scales of 1:25,000 and 1:50,000.» Here mapping means making maps of an area.
explain: The -ing ending gives you a clue too. In «we are mapping the playground», mapping is a verb. It shows that people are doing the action of map right now. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or is someone doing something?
explain: Use the topic to choose the meaning. If the sentence is about maps, roads or land, it means making maps. If it is about numbers, arrows or sets, it is the maths meaning. If it is about planning ideas on paper, it means a diagram that shows how things are connected, like a mind mapping activity.
fact: As a noun, mapping means the making of maps of an area.
fact: As a verb, mapping is the -ing form of map, as in «we are mapping the playground».
fact: In maths, a mapping is a rule that links each item in one set to an item in another set, like each number to its double.
fact: A mind mapping activity is a plan or diagram that shows how ideas are connected.
fact: «Mapping out» means planning, and «map out a route» means plan the way to go.
exercise: «Great Britain's national mapping agency makes detailed maps.» What does mapping mean here? | Walking slowly around a park | *The making of maps of an area | A rule linking each number to its double | A plan showing how ideas connect
exercise: Ella says mapping in a maths lesson means drawing a picture of a playground. What is a mapping in maths? | Cutting paper into shapes | *A rule that links each item in one set to an item in another set | Drawing a picture of a playground | A list of the longest words
exercise: «We are mapping the playground.» Why is mapping a verb here? | *It is the -ing form of map, so the action is happening now | It is a noun naming a place | It is a plan for next week | It means the same as the playground
test: «The app used mapping to show the quickest route home.» What does mapping mean here? | *Making a diagram or map that shows where to go | Painting a picture of the town | Counting the steps to school | A rule linking numbers to their doubles
test: «Jamal drew a mind mapping diagram to plan his story.» What is a mind mapping diagram? | *A diagram that shows how ideas are connected | A machine that measures the land | A map of the ocean floor | A list of maths rules
exam: «The teacher said, "Before we write, let us map out our ideas."» What does map out mean here? | Count the words in the story | Draw a map of the school | Throw our ideas away | *Plan our ideas in an organised way
